From: Gale <gale@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hoist inOpenSet + skip getBestH on update (Gale #203 part)

Port of GaleMC/Gale #203 hot-loop part against our tree (adapted:
our tree uses localOpenSet/localNeighbors via async pathfinding).
Caches inOpenSet() and skips getBestH when only updating cost.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathFinder.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathFinder.java
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathFinder.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathFinder.java
@@ -165,15 +165,16 @@ public class PathFinder {
                     float distance = this.distance(current, neighbor);
                     neighbor.walkedDistance = current.walkedDistance + distance;
                     float tentativeGScore = current.g + distance + neighbor.costMalus;
-                    if (neighbor.walkedDistance < maxPathLength && (!neighbor.inOpenSet() || tentativeGScore < neighbor.g)) {
+                    boolean inOpenSet = neighbor.inOpenSet(); // Gale - reduce pathfinding overhead - hoist inOpenSet out of condition
+                    if (neighbor.walkedDistance < maxPathLength && (!inOpenSet || tentativeGScore < neighbor.g)) {
                         neighbor.cameFrom = current;
                         neighbor.g = tentativeGScore;
-                        neighbor.h = this.getBestH(neighbor, targets) * 1.5F;
-                        if (neighbor.inOpenSet()) {
+                        if (inOpenSet) {
                             localOpenSet.changeCost(neighbor, neighbor.g + neighbor.h); // Kaiiju - petal - async path processing
                         } else {
+                            neighbor.h = this.getBestH(neighbor, targets) * 1.5F; // Gale - reduce pathfinding overhead - skip getBestH on cost update
                             neighbor.f = neighbor.g + neighbor.h;
                             localOpenSet.insert(neighbor); // Kaiiju - petal - async path processing
                         }

